Welcome home. You are kitty, and /usr/kitty is yours.

Three real toolchains (boot the developer world for all of them):
  cc hello.c ; ./a.out         real clang + wasm-ld — flags, -o, -c, -E, -S
  go run hello.go              THE REAL Go compiler, running in this tab
  go build hello.go ; ./hello  same, keeping the binary; go fmt works too
  python hello.py              real CPython 3.14

Install packages — pip speaks to the real PyPI:
  pip install cowsay
  python -c 'import cowsay; cowsay.cow("Hello Kitty")'
  pip list / show / uninstall  (pure-Python wheels; python -m pip works)

The example programs from python.org and gobyexample.com run as written —
try goroutines, channels, generics, text/template, regexp, json.

Look around:
  ls /bin        the commands            cal    this month
  cat /etc/motd | tr a-z A-Z             ls /lib/python3.14 | wc -l

Windows and editors:
  win acme &     the real acme (option-click = button 2)
  win rc &       another shell, in a window

The whole tour:  rc /rc/tour
Everything runs in this browser tab. A reload forgets it all.
